{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01N7ChfuYWgzN11ZHXGqte12","type":"tool_result","content":"18:- Never delete world save files such as server-world.dat, server-players.dat, or similar without explicit user permission.\n20:- For 1.7.6 SpawnPlayer (0x0C), write VarInt(0) for the properties count.\n55:- For Beta BlockPlacement packets, use `PlayerBlockPlacementPacketBeta`.\n58:- When sending packets to a v45 client during early login, send PlayStatus(LOGIN_SUCCESS) as a standalone packet, not batched.\n59:- When serializing the 1.7.2 SpawnPlayer packet (0x0C), omit the properties list.\n78:- For Beta clients, implement Q-drops with PlayerDigging status=4 instead of using PickupSpawn.\n85:- In the cross-test scenario, call setLookDirection to make the player face the other player before taking the screenshot.\n92:- When spawning a player for 1.8 clients, send PlayerListItem ADD_PLAYER before SpawnPlayer so the client can resolve the name from the tab list.\n96:- For Beta 1.8 server list ping (0xFE), respond with 0xFF followed by String16(\"motd§players§max\") and then close the connection.\n127:- For player despawn, use REMOVE_ENTITY (0x0C) instead of REMOVE_PLAYER.\n146:- Never reset world save files such as server-world.dat, server-players.dat, or similar without explicit user permission.\n150:- Rotate to face the other player.\n159:- Send AddPlayer, StartGame, and MovePlayer S2C Y at feet-level.\n169:- Before any destructive file operation (rm, overwrite, reset) on data files in the project root—including world saves, player data, configuration, and any non-code files that may contain user-generated state—always ask the user first.\n181:- In VerifyGroundStep, when settleTicks==0, call gs.offsetPlayerX(-5.0) to nudge the player away from the column before taking the screenshot.\n189:- Use `PlayerController.b.a(int,int,int,int)` direct dig packets to bypass `Minecraft.a(0)` cooldown and objectMouseOver checks.\n206:- Raycast from the player's eye position along the look direction.\n221:- Treat MCPE C2S MovePlayer Y as feet-level and the internal server Y as eye-level (feet + 1.62).\n232:- Never reset world save files such as server-world.dat, server-players.dat, or similar without explicit user permission.\n247:- Do not implement PlayerAbilities (0xCA) for Beta 1.8; take abilities from the `gameMode` field in Login/Respawn.\n255:- For v768 PlayerInput (SteerVehicle), encode the packet as a single byte flags field; do not use the old float sideways + float forward + byte flags format.\n270:- For 1.8+ clients, subtract PLAYER_EYE_HEIGHT from the internal eye-level Y when sending player position in both handleJoinGame() and respawnToSafePosition().\n298:- Always include the speedX, speedY, and speedZ fields when writing AddPlayerPacket (0x07).\n303:- Disable the raycast Animate handler for protocol v14 and above, since those clients send PlayerAction.\n314:- Delete all map and player data as part of pre-test setup.\n315:- For Beta 1.8 (v17) BlockPlacement, use `short damage` in `PlayerBlockPlacementPacketV17`, not `byte`.\n318:- Never delete world save files such as server-world.dat, server-players.dat, or similar without explicit user permission.\n371:- Use a direct posX field write rather than forcePlayerPosition to move the player, to avoid Entity.a()→move() issues on Alpha 1.2.2+.\n396:- In handleJoinGame(), call ClassicToNettyTranslator.setClientVersion() before broadcastPlayerListAdd() and broadcastPlayerSpawn()."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ae76414d-108e-4c73-a392-f12f014eafe3","uuid":"b2618e8c-389e-43c1-a061-d09937ee988e","timestamp":"2026-11-25T02:55:53.725Z","tool_use_result":{"mode":"content","numFiles":0,"filenames":[],"content":"18:- Never delete world save files such as server-world.dat, server-players.dat, or similar without explicit user permission.\n20:- For 1.7.6 SpawnPlayer (0x0C), write VarInt(0) for the properties count.\n55:- For Beta BlockPlacement packets,